# News Aggregator API

A RESTful API built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB that supports user authentication, personalized news preferences, and news retrieval.

## Features

- User signup and login with bcrypt password hashing.
- JWT-based authentication.
- Get and update user preferences.
- Fetch news using NewsAPI.
- MongoDB integration with Mongoose.

## Tech Stack

Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, Mongoose, JWT, bcrypt, NewsAPI.

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/rajivk5/news-aggregator.git
cd news-aggregator
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```env
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
NEWS_API_KEY=your_news_api_key
```

## Run the Project

```bash
npm start
```

The server runs on `http://localhost:3000`.

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint             | Description               |
| ------ | -------------------- | ------------------------- |
| POST   | `/users/signup`      | Register a user           |
| POST   | `/users/login`       | Log in and receive a JWT  |
| GET    | `/users/preferences` | Get user preferences      |
| PUT    | `/users/preferences` | Update user preferences   |
| GET    | `/news`              | Fetch news (JWT required) |

For protected endpoints, send the token in the header:

```text
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token>
```

## Run Tests

```bash
npm run test
```

## Security

Never commit your `.env` file or expose API keys, database credentials, or JWT secrets.
